Ranged weapons are those that can be used against creatures in rooms other than
the one you are presently in.  The common forms are bows with their ammunition,
and certain thrown weapons such as daggers and axes.

Ranged weapons do respectable damage on impact, but the real worth of a pointed
one is that it embeds itself in its target.  An embedded missile goes on doing
harm long after the shot - it can tear further when pulled out badly, and a
wound left with something in it will fester.  How readily a missile lodges
depends on how sharp it still is, so ammunition that has seen hard use bites
less well than it did when new.

Not everything that flies has a point.  Blunt ammunition batters instead,
leaving deep bruising rather than a puncture, and armour matters far more
against it than sharpness ever could.

Ranged weapons cannot be used in a peaceful room, nor against a target in one.
Some rooms are off-limits to mobs, and a shot cannot pass through such a room.

Thrown weapons have short range and modest damage but need little training.
Bows shoot further and hit harder, at the cost of needing the right ammunition
for the bow, and sometimes the strength to draw it.  A missile's damage comes
from its own quality, the training of whoever loosed it, and - for the heavier
bows - the strength behind the draw.

Specialization in ranged weapons improves accuracy and damage alike, and allows
more than one shot in a round.

